      en: "The Yantra River Valley runs through northern Bulgaria. The Yantra River, 285 km long, originates in the Balkan Mountains and flows into the Danube. The valley is narrow with steep slopes. It is famous for vineyards and the medieval capital Veliko Tarnovo. The region supports diverse birdlife, including white storks. Agriculture focuses on wine and fruit. The valley was a strategic trade route during the Second Bulgarian Empire. Rock formations near Dryanovo are notable. Tourism blends history and nature.",
