      en: "The Balkan Gorges are deep canyons cutting through the Balkan Mountains in a north-south direction. The most famous is the Iskar Gorge, stretching about 70 km from Lakatnik to Novi Iskar. The gorge exposes a continuous sequence of Mesozoic limestone, with cliffs rising up to 300 m. It serves as a major transport route for the Sofia-Varna railway and highway. The area is a hotspot for climbing and caving, with over 100 caves. The Duhlata cave is one of the longest in Bulgaria at 18 km. The gorge is also an Important Bird Area, hosting the peregrine falcon and golden eagle.",
