      en: "The Stara Planina Plateau is a high karst plateau in the eastern Balkan Mountains, at 1000-1500 m elevation. Underlain by Jurassic and Cretaceous limestones, it features typical karst landforms: sinkholes, uvalas, and blind valleys. Soils are thin, supporting grasslands and scrub used for sheep grazing. The plateau has several hunting reserves for red deer and wild boar. Winters are snowy with temperatures dropping below -10°C; summers are mild. The town of Teteven (pop. 10,000) is the main settlement. The ”Kozya Stena” reserve protects a population of Balkan chamois.",
