      en: "The Rhodope Ridge is the main ridge of the Rhodope Mountains, stretching about 150 km west-east. Its highest peaks are Golyam Perelik (2191 m) and Shumnatica (2186 m). The terrain is Alpine, shaped by Pleistocene glaciers, with sharp arêtes and cirques. Forests of Scots pine and Norway spruce dominate up to 1800 m, followed by alpine meadows. The ridge is within the Rhodope Nature Park. Notable landmarks include the Trigrad Gorge (300 m deep) and the Devil's Bridge. The area is known for its preserved 19th-century villages and mineral springs.",
